Source: https://github.com/greg-kennedy/libsmacker
Revision: 76094fb9c8e98bd5fac982c504e8d9aeff3ece01
Local changes: allocation failure unwinds instead of terminating the process;
null-safe partial cleanup; PCM words use explicit little-endian byte access;
bounded palette/audio chunks with decode-error propagation; palette scratch
is local to each decode rather than shared static storage. Status/read/bit
results use int so failures stay negative with unsigned plain char targets.
The preserved Smacker32/oracle builds are not changed.
